WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.819 --> 00:00:02.920
Film Courage: How do you write a great scene?

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.060
Shannan E. Johnson, Writer/Instructor/Script
Consultant: I think you should look at your

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:11.570
scenes like you look at the whole screenplay
and figure out the cause and effect of what

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:19.480
does this scene cause to happen and how is
it the effect of what happened before it?

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:25.470
Understanding that in every scene there is
a goal just like there is in the entire screenplay.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.869
The only reason we are seeing this scene is
because it’s getting you closer to or further

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:32.529
away from your goal.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:37.880
If you look at it like there is a goal that
has to be reached so that you can get to the

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.670
next thing that gets to the next thing that
gets to the next thing.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:45.860
Then you end up not having scenes that are
back to just regular activity instead of intentional

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.789
action or even considering from an actor’s
point of view when they are going to play

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:53.180
out that scene one of them is winning right?

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:58.059
Somebody is going to win in this thing (in
this scene) it’s kind of like it’s a fight.

00:00:58.059 --> 00:00:59.059
Ding!

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.059
Ding!

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:01.059
Ding!

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:03.629
In this corner these characters are going
to come and whatever it is that they are saying

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:07.090
to each other someone is going to win emotionally,
someone is going to lose.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.110
Someone might physically win, someone might
lose.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:13.090
But what that means is now that emotional
journey that I was on has been changed.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.860
Again, it’s the cause and effect.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.290
So there might by a physical cause and effect,
it might be an emotional cause and effect

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.700
or it might be both.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.729
But looking at the scenes like they are little
movies right?

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:25.070
Like what is it setting up for me?

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:28.860
What is the goal of this scene and then how
does it resolve to get me to the next thing.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:33.159
Film Courage: So if we were going to take
the hypothetical female character who was

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:42.270
entering a singing contest, now she nows that
her mother needs this deposit to start treatment…so

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:46.140
that great scene is going to be her maybe
getting this news?

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:51.040
Then she knows that the contest is coming
up and all of the things she has to do to

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.040
prepare?

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.040
I don’t know…because the stakes have risen.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.110
It’s not just “Oh I need it for my dorm
room.”

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:56.430
Or “I want to buy a nice purse.”

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:01.300
Shannan: Yes, so now her action because of
that scene, because of that new information,

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.770
her intentional action is going to change.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.219
Maybe before then she wasn’t practicing
very much because she’s got a natural voice

00:02:07.219 --> 00:02:08.219
you know?

00:02:08.219 --> 00:02:11.320
She wasn’t practicing very much, she wasn’t
finding any new songs, she’s like “Oh

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.660
yeah, I’ll just go up there and I will sing.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.760
Whatever, because every time I sing a song
it’s great.”

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:19.160
But now this thing has been a humbling moment
for her.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.870
Now we are going to see her going to her lessons.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.750
We’re going to see her trying to find the
best song, she is going to be putting a different

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.830
kind of action into it because now the stakes
are risen.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:33.310
Now there is something more at stake so she’s
going to put a different kind of action into

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:34.310
it.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.280
That thing is going to cause her to change.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.190
Exactly.

